# Agent ships; Joseph does not carry git burden

When the agent finishes a task that changes the repo, **commit, push, and land on `main`** in the same piece of work. Do not leave uncommitted fixes or ask Joseph to commit or merge unless credentials or policy block the ship.

## Always

- Resolve merge conflicts locally (stash/move local-only files if needed, `git pull --rebase` or `--ff-only`, reconcile, test).
- Keep **one active line of truth: `main`** synced with `origin/main` after ship.
- For Studio Web / Worker changes, append deploy trigger files and bump BUILD_ID / Worker version per `ship-studio-pages-worker.mdc`.
- Prefer a PR when cloud/branch workflow requires it: open the PR, wait for CI green, **mark ready and merge it yourself** (squash), then sync local `main`. Do not stop at “ready for you to merge.”
- Push to `origin/main` after commit when direct-to-main is allowed; otherwise merge the PR as above.

## Never

- Stop with “ready to commit when you want” or “merge when ready.”
- Leave WIP on `main` unpushed after claiming a fix is done.
- Force-push `main` without explicit Joseph request.

## Secrets

- Do not commit `.env`, credentials, or local-only watchdog backups (`*.local.vbs`, `*.localbak`, personal task XML exports).
